    "field": "Antarctic climate science",
    "problem": "The physical processes and large-scale atmospheric drivers of sporadic but extensive surface melt events over the West Antarctic Ice Sheet are not fully understood, a problem compounded by their infrequent occurrence and a lack of comprehensive on-site observations.",
    "method": "This study investigates an extensive West Antarctic melt event by combining satellite data, comprehensive in-situ atmospheric measurements from the AWARE field campaign, and idealized climate model simulations to attribute the event's cause to a strong El Ni\u00f1o and associated warm air advection.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the physical processes and large-scale atmospheric drivers, particularly the strong El Ni\u00f1o event, responsible for the extensive and prolonged surface melting observed over a large sector of the West Antarctic Ice Sheet in January 2016 using satellite, in-situ, and model data.",
